### CST8917 Assignment 2 — Version B: Logic Apps + Service Bus
### Expense Approval Workflow — test scenarios
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
###
### Flow under test:
###   POST /api/expenses (Azure Function)
###     -> enqueues onto Service Bus queue "expense-requests"
###     -> Logic App trigger picks it up
###     -> Validate_Expense action calls /api/validate
###     -> auto-approve, or Wait_For_Manager_Decision webhook (see below)
###     -> outcome published to topic "expense-outcomes" with filtered
###        subscriptions (approved-sub / rejected-sub / escalated-sub /
###        validation-error-sub) and an email is sent.
###
### Replace {functionAppUrl} with your deployed Function App base URL
### (or http://localhost:7071 for local testing with `func start`),
### and include the function key if running with AuthLevel.FUNCTION
### against a deployed app (?code=...).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7071/api

### ============================================================
### Scenario 1: Valid expense under $100 -> Auto-approved
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Alice Chen",
  "employeeEmail": "alice.chen@example.com",
  "amount": 45.50,
  "category": "supplies",
  "description": "Notebooks and pens for the team",
  "managerEmail": "manager1@example.com"
}

### Verify: Logic App run history shows Condition_Amount_Under_100 = true
### branch; a message with application property outcome=approved lands in
### 'approved-sub'; employee receives an "approved" email.


### ============================================================
### Scenario 2: Valid expense >= $100, manager approves -> Approved
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Bilal Karim",
  "employeeEmail": "bilal.karim@example.com",
  "amount": 350.00,
  "category": "travel",
  "description": "Flight to client site",
  "managerEmail": "manager1@example.com"
}

### While the Logic App run is paused on Wait_For_Manager_Decision, open
### the run in the portal (or check Application Insights / the Function
### log for notify-manager) and copy the `callbackUrl` value that was sent
### to /api/notify-manager. Paste it below, then send this request BEFORE
### the managerTimeout (default PT5M) elapses.
POST PASTE_CALLBACK_URL_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approved"
}


### ============================================================
### Scenario 3: Valid expense >= $100, manager rejects -> Rejected
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Carla Diaz",
  "employeeEmail": "carla.diaz@example.com",
  "amount": 899.99,
  "category": "equipment",
  "description": "New monitor",
  "managerEmail": "manager1@example.com"
}

### Copy the callbackUrl from the run's Wait_For_Manager_Decision action
POST PASTE_CALLBACK_URL_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "rejected"
}


### ============================================================
### Scenario 4: Valid expense >= $100, no manager response -> Escalated
### Do NOT call the callback URL for this instance.
### Wait for managerTimeout (default 5 min); Wait_For_Manager_Decision
### times out, Compose_Escalated_Outcome/Publish_Escalated_To_Topic run.
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Deepa Nair",
  "employeeEmail": "deepa.nair@example.com",
  "amount": 500.00,
  "category": "software",
  "description": "Annual IDE license",
  "managerEmail": "manager1@example.com"
}

### Verify: message with outcome=escalated lands in 'escalated-sub';
### employee receives an "auto-approved (escalated)" email.


### ============================================================
### Scenario 5: Missing required fields -> Validation error
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Evan Wright",
  "amount": 75,
  "category": "meals",
  "description": "Team lunch"
}

### Missing employeeEmail and managerEmail.
### Verify: Validate_Expense returns valid=false; Condition_Is_Valid takes
### the "else" branch; message with outcome=validation_error lands in
### 'validation-error-sub'.


### ============================================================
### Scenario 6: Invalid category -> Validation error
### ============================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/expenses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeName": "Fiona Lee",
  "employeeEmail": "fiona.lee@example.com",
  "amount": 120,
  "category": "entertainment",
  "description": "Client dinner",
  "managerEmail": "manager1@example.com"
}

### "entertainment" is not in the valid category list.
### Verify: same validation_error path as Scenario 5.
